# Gitignored files copied into every Claude Code worktree at creation.
# Syntax: .gitignore-style. Only files that match AND are gitignored are copied.
# Docs: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/worktrees#copy-gitignored-files-into-worktrees
#
# .mcp.json is REQUIRED, not just convenient: the Bash sandbox (bwrap) bind-mounts
# <cwd>/.mcp.json as a mountpoint. In a worktree under the read-only .claude/ tree it
# cannot CREATE that mountpoint, so a missing .mcp.json aborts sandbox setup and kills
# EVERY Bash command with:
#   bwrap: Can't create file at <worktree>/.mcp.json: Read-only file system
# worktree.sparsePaths cannot fix this — sparse-checkout delivers tracked files only.
.mcp.json

# DELIBERATELY NOT INCLUDED — do not "helpfully" re-add:
#   .env  — carries live secrets/tokens. Copying it duplicates them into EVERY new
#           worktree, including automatically-created agent worktrees, with no
#           lifecycle management. .mcp.json is required to prevent a hard sandbox
#           outage; .env is only a convenience, so the risk is not worth it.
#           If a worktree needs it, copy it deliberately for that worktree.
